# --output-dir does not write over a file it formats: the directory holding
# it is refused for that file, exit 1, and nothing is written.
program Opp
arg --output-dir
arg tests/data/
arg tests/data/formatted.Mod
status 1
output
opp: --output-dir would write over tests/data/formatted.Mod itself, so nothing is written for it (--in-place formats a file in place)
